  "assumptions": [
    "Primary keys are uuid surrogate keys named id; junction tables (product_categories, product_occasions) use their own surrogate id plus a unique composite index on the two FK columns so each table has exactly one primary key column.",
    "Composite indexes are written as comma-separated column names; entries marked (unique) must be created as unique indexes.",
    "A single users table with a role column (customer, courier, admin) models all three roles; role values are enforced by a CHECK constraint or enum in the application layer.",
    "Orders are created only after successful Stripe payment; failed payment attempts are stored in payments with a null order_id so no order exists for them.",
    "Card data is never stored; only the Stripe payment intent id is kept (PCI-DSS delegated to Stripe).",
    "Orders snapshot the delivery address and item prices so history stays correct if saved addresses or product prices change; reordering reads product_id from order_items and adds items to the cart at current prices.",
    "Product availability is derived (is_active = true and stock_quantity > 0) rather than stored; out-of-stock products cannot be added to the cart (enforced in application logic).",
    "Each order has at most one delivery/courier assignment; reassignment updates the deliveries row, and the order_status_history table keeps the full timeline.",
    "Address and contact fields are encrypted at rest (column-level or disk-level); on account deletion request, personal data is purged or anonymized within 30 days using deletion_requested_at, while order records are retained in anonymized form.",
    "Passwords are stored as bcrypt hashes in users.password_hash.",
    "Monetary amounts use decimal(10,2) with a single currency per order (default USD); timestamps are stored in UTC.",
    "Soft removal of products uses is_active = false so historical order_items keep valid references."
  ]
}